{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And the right thigh.</b> Rashi wrote: we find no burning of the right thigh with the innards except this one alone. That is, it is the thigh of the ram of ordination of the first day, but of the other six rams that were offered on the other days of ordination, no thigh was burned from them. And this is what Rashi explains shortly after: I require the breast to belong to him who performs the service, as a portion." "<b>For it is a ram of ordination.</b> Because with it their hands were filled, and this gives the reason why this thigh is burned."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:01:04.001254978Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}